WEBVTT


00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.274
You don't know
where you're going.


00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.217
Yes, I do.


00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:57.620
- You don't know where you are.
- Yes, I do. I'm in hell.


00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:02.923
Just get in the car.
You cannot walk the entire way to...


00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:07.158
- This was your choice.
- This was not my choice, Mom.


00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:11.761
What, to live with some old bitch that you
can't even stand that I don't even know?


00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.602
You wanted me out of your life,
I'm out of your life, Mom.


00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.074
You're impossible. You are impossible.


00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.338
If you weren't such a nutcase,


00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.870
we could have flown here like normal
people and been done with this shit.


00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.407
You won, OK? You won.
I'm out of your life.


00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.546
- No one has won.
- I'm out of your life.


00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.750
Now if you please would just get out of mine.


00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.556
- Go. Get out.
- All right, fine.


00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.089
Hello?


00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.536
Hey! Whoa!


00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.275
Whoa, whoa! Hey, hey, hey!


00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.011
Who are you?


00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.553
Hey, I didn't mean nothing.
Just calm down.


00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:12.079
My God, are you one of those
back-country sodomy boys?


00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.820
I didn't mean any harm.


00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.227
Can you help me up, please?


00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.296
- Are you crazy?
- No.


00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.233
I'm Rachel.


00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.000
Harlan Wilson.


00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.837
You got yourself a nice feel there,
didn't you, Harlan Wilson?


00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.242
- Hey, that wasn't my intention.
- What were your intentions?


00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:36.111
To see if you were dead.


00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.843
Car trouble, Harlan?


00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.547
Hey, I had one of these.
Till I crashed it. Can I drive?


00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:48.060
- Beg your pardon?
- I found her sleeping by the side of the road.


00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.857
Come on, let's go. Let's go.


00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.330
- Says her name's Rachel.
- Yeah?


00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:57.199
If she turns out to be sane...
you know, she's all yours.


00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.535
- I gotta get back to work.
- Hey.


00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:04.634
Is for horses. Better for cows.
Pigs don't eat it 'cause they don't know how.


00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:07.908
- What's your name?
- Simon.


00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.913
Hmm.


00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.682
- I wasn't really going anywhere.
- That's where I'm going.


00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.878
- Where?
- Anywhere.


00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:17.116
- I was going there alone.
- Now you're not. Consider yourself lucky.


00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.718
- I would if you weren't here.
- Mm. Consider yourself stuck.


00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:30.964
- I don't like to talk.
- Perfect. I don't like to listen.


00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:45.147
- Would you put your legs back in my car?
- Changing the rules?


00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:49.678
There were no rules. Other than no
parts of your body outside my car.


00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.782
- Well, then, can I talk to you?
- Put your legs down.


00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:55.794
You didn't say "Simon says," Simon.


00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:02.191
- I'm only going as far as Hull.
- Hull, Idaho? That's where I'm staying.


00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.395
My luck.


00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.837
Now, do you need to call someone,
or are you a surprise?


00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:13.106
I would. My mother cut my phone service off.
She's a gem.


00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:50.939
Nuh-uh. Ace is only low.
Not high. Georgia rule.


00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:54.009
Everybody else plays the right way.
Why can't we?


00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:59.286
So if everybody took a poop in the middle of Main
Street you'd do it too? 'Cause they said it was right?


00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.953
- Probably.
- My leg is numb.


00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:04.462
Hey, no quitting.


00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.158
I got pains from my gluteus
shooting up and out my eyes


00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:10.259
from sitting on the floor
with two boneless children.


00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:13.203
Quitting?
Did you hear me say "quitting"?


00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:26.982
Rummy.


00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.578
Uhh.


00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:33.022
- Mom?
- Wait. No, we can't go. I'm winning.


00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.751
- Hello. You're not Mom.
- Hello.


00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.264
Lilly. Come on in.


00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:49.797
- Come on, boys. Erect me.
- She has gluten pains shooting out her eyeballs.


00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.482
Where's Rachel?


00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:05.548
I thought this drive would be good for us. That
we could talk, at least tolerate each other.


00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.025
Where is my granddaughter?


00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:11.427
She bolted from the car.


00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.402
You look really nice, anyway, Lilly.


00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:22.236
I should have put her on a plane.


00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.640
- Still smoke?
- No.


00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:29.947
Did I ask if you still dye your hair? I haven't
had a drink in years, in case you wanted to know.


00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:33.247
- It's none of my business.
- Yeah? Heh-heh.


00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:35.378
I brought you a gift.


00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:38.424
- Oh, it's lovely.
- How do you know?


00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:42.621
The ribbon and the paper. How's she gonna
find me? She's only been here once.


00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:45.721
13 years ago. Same as you.


00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:50.565
Rachel is very resourceful.
She'll find you when she needs you.


00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.695
Why are children in your house?


00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:57.141
They're my friends. Here, guys.
I watch them till their mom gets home.


00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.235
This is Sam. This is Ethan.


00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.179
- Nice to meet you.
- This is my daughter Lilly.


00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:03.476
Hi.


00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:10.355
Traveled all the way from San Francisco, California,
smelling of smoke. But she doesn't smoke.


00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.254
OK, Mother, caught me.


00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.522
Save the lies for something
more important than cancer.


00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:18.689
Why don't you go get the bags, you two?


00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:22.894
Oh, um, you know what?
Everything but the Louis Vuittons.


00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:26.200
They have "LV" written all over 'em.


00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:32.867
- You travel with luggage you don't use?
- Oh, I'm just staying a minute.


00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:37.678
I have friends. They're begging me
to come down to Salt Lake City and visit.


00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.184
Good friends?


00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.778
We keep in touch.


00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.323
Well, it's worth the drive, then.


00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:50.729
Bringing up the girl's bags.


00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.128
I think they got rocks in 'em.


00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:02.800
Everything's exactly the same,
except for the bird.


00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:08.641
It's a glass... bedpan?


00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.979
Heh-heh. Crystal bowl. It's classy.


00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:16.250
- I thought of one for my mantel.
- Take this one, then.


00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:18.950
It's a gift, Mother.


00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:22.660
It's just there's so much on my mantel.


00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:26.061
Well, look around,
because I'm not taking it back.


00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:27.497
Thank you.


00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:30.968
It's lovely. Nice, thanks.


00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:36.932
- Well, this is Hull.
- Just drop me in town. Nice to know you, Simon.


00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:39.671
- You don't know me, kid.
- I know you.


00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:41.906
You do?


00:09:42.648 --> 00:09:45.879
I had my dress hiked and my legs up,
and you didn't look once.


00:09:45.952 --> 00:09:48.546
Not even for a second.


00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:50.816
So now you know me?


00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.792
No marriage ring.
What are you, 30? 40?


00:09:55.361 --> 00:09:57.352
You're gay.


00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:06.838
- All right, get out.
- I already asked you to let me out.


00:10:06.906 --> 00:10:11.843
- I'm telling you.
- What? You can't tell me what I've already asked.


00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:14.744
Get out. Just get out.


00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:21.152
I want my panties back
when you're done with them.


00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:27.057
Harlan found her sleeping
by the side of the road.


00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:30.562
- Do you buy that?
- He's a wonderful doctor.


00:10:48.014 --> 00:10:51.814
- Thanks for the sandwich.
- You won't make it to your friends' before dark.


00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:56.184
- That wasn't really my goal.
- Accidents mostly happen at dusk.


00:10:56.255 --> 00:11:00.191
- I would guess morning.
- Well, you'd be wrong.


00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:02.659
All in God's hands.


00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:05.561
- That's what your father always used to say.
- Uh-huh.


00:11:05.631 --> 00:11:08.065
Everybody's hands but his own.


00:11:09.101 --> 00:11:12.127
You never said anything bad about him
when he was alive.


00:11:12.204 --> 00:11:15.332
Well, if I did, why would I say it to you?


00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:21.739
Why say anything? Your granddaughter
takes off when she doesn't get her way.


00:11:21.814 --> 00:11:24.647
She's easy to find, though.
Just listen for a scream.


00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:30.713
If she doesn't show up in the next few hours,
call me on my cellphone, I'll turn around.


00:11:32.792 --> 00:11:35.192
Thank you for taking her.


00:11:35.561 --> 00:11:38.155
I hope it does her some good.


00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.698
Did it do you any good?


00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:41.553
- Ahem. You don't look evil.
- Makeup helps.


00:12:41.627 --> 00:12:45.996
- Hmm. Where's my mom?
- Had to see friends.


00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.794
Oh, right.


00:12:47.867 --> 00:12:53.601
Did you hear the one where she's stopped
smoking, drinking and hating herself, too?


00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.871
Rachel...


00:13:06.152 --> 00:13:08.416
I'm hungry.
Got anything with sugar?


00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:10.887
You're five hours late.


00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:14.653
My mother dumped me 20 miles out.
I had to walk the whole way.


00:13:14.727 --> 00:13:17.628
We eat at six. No exceptions.


00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:20.221
You'll have to wait for breakfast.


00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:23.132
Oh, there's apples on the table.


00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:28.972
Mm. Can I tell you what's really going on?
So we don't get lost in what this really is.


00:13:29.041 --> 00:13:31.874
I'd like to know.


00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:37.115
My mother and stepfather don't like my life.
Maybe because I have one, who knows?


00:13:37.183 --> 00:13:40.744
Anyway, I was stupid enough
to graduate high school in January.


00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:46.452
I got into a trouble a few times while I was waiting to
go to college in the fall. So they had to get rid of me.


00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:49.187
Banished for the summer in Idaho.


00:13:49.261 --> 00:13:53.163
Locked up with the one person on earth
my mother can't jerk around.


00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:55.257
That's why I'm here.


00:13:55.334 --> 00:13:57.928
Try and jerk me around, Grandma.


00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:08.875
Go fuck yourself.


00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.542
No good night kiss?


00:14:15.888 --> 00:14:16.946
OK.


00:15:11.777 --> 00:15:15.907
You know, the only picture
I've ever seen of you is with me in it.


00:15:15.981 --> 00:15:18.677
Holding this dog.


00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:22.881
I got it for you so you wouldn't be afraid
at your grandfather's funeral.


00:15:22.955 --> 00:15:25.185
You named it Grandpa.


00:15:25.257 --> 00:15:29.421
I was four. Couldn't you have helped me
pick a name that made some sense?


00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:32.089
It made sense to you.


00:15:33.732 --> 00:15:36.792
My stepfather promised
to buy me a new car for school.


00:15:36.869 --> 00:15:40.100
You know, if I can survive up here,
stay sane.


00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:43.801
Oh. So your time here
won't be a complete waste.


00:15:43.876 --> 00:15:46.242
Well, I'll miss my friends.


00:15:46.312 --> 00:15:51.511
Oh, cheer up. Most friends, in time,
become as useless as relatives.


00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:11.226
So, I brought seven novels. If I read them slowly,
that should kill two of the ten weeks that I'm here.


00:16:12.071 --> 00:16:14.539
Oh, my God, what is that?


00:16:15.808 --> 00:16:18.572
I don't want you
to take the Lord's name in vain.


00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:22.102
The f-you lady won't let me say "Oh, my God"?
Got any sugar?


00:16:22.181 --> 00:16:24.741
I will not tolerate blasphemy.


00:16:25.751 --> 00:16:28.379
And the next time,
I want you to sleep upstairs.


00:16:28.454 --> 00:16:32.254
- What if I want to take a nap?
- Upstairs. Georgia rule.


00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:34.519
God, lady, you are weird.


00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:38.558
I will wash your mouth out next time.


00:16:40.499 --> 00:16:42.865
No wonder Mom hates you.


00:16:46.238 --> 00:16:49.207
I'm glad you're here, Rachel.


00:16:54.213 --> 00:17:00.345
So, do you guys have anything better
around here than Harlan Wilson?


00:17:01.353 --> 00:17:03.583
Keep your dress on. I got you a job.


00:17:04.356 --> 00:17:06.654
- A what?
- It starts Monday.


00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:09.751
Just a brisk walk from here.
I'll wake you at seven.


00:17:09.828 --> 00:17:12.661
- I'm not working.
- One more rule.


00:17:12.731 --> 00:17:16.724
- You live here, you work.
- OK...


00:17:16.802 --> 00:17:21.830
I know that you pulled your "Georgia rule"
bullshit with my mother before she fled.


00:17:21.907 --> 00:17:25.172
But I'm not her.
And you can't tell me what to do.


00:17:25.244 --> 00:17:27.974
Rachel rule.


00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:30.345
Wash your dishes.


00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:32.611
Are you asking or telling?


00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:35.551
You finished, wash your dishes.


00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:44.757
I've never really washed a dish before.


00:17:57.409 --> 00:18:01.004
Morning. How are you?
Have you been practicing?


00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:17.157
I don't know if I can afford this one.
It's for Izzy.


00:18:17.229 --> 00:18:20.596
I'm trying to find something easier
on his back. I saw something...


00:18:28.574 --> 00:18:29.632
Hey.


00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:37.277
- Morning.
- Morning.


00:18:44.823 --> 00:18:47.951
Surprise.
Saddling up your truck?


00:18:48.026 --> 00:18:51.962
I had it figured
that you'd done away with Simon,


00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:55.864
buried his body and taken off for the city
with his cash and car.


00:18:55.934 --> 00:18:58.095
And leave you alive?


00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.938
Just how disturbed are you?


00:19:01.006 --> 00:19:03.634
I prefer "unique. "


00:19:03.709 --> 00:19:06.678
- How old are you, anyway?
- Old enough.


00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:10.170
- Old enough for what?
- To disturb you.


00:19:11.316 --> 00:19:14.683
You're a dangerous girl, aren't you?


00:19:14.753 --> 00:19:17.119
It depends on what you consider dangerous.


00:19:17.189 --> 00:19:19.817
Safer to get thrown from a horse.


00:19:19.892 --> 00:19:24.955
Well, you don't have to brush or feed me
after riding me.


00:19:31.303 --> 00:19:34.272
I got a girl.


00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:39.441
Have a good day, cowboy.


00:19:45.184 --> 00:19:47.846
Fourth of July picnic this Saturday.


00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.320
Bring the family.


00:19:50.389 --> 00:19:54.189
- Mandy, stop us.
- Mark time. March.


00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:57.558
- Who is that?
- I don't know.


00:19:57.629 --> 00:20:00.530
Not from around here.
Move us.


00:20:00.599 --> 00:20:02.692
Forward, march.


00:20:02.768 --> 00:20:05.066
Fourth of July picnic this Saturday.


00:20:05.137 --> 00:20:08.163
Music and games.
Petting zoo for the kids.


00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:11.676
Pet a cow. Squeeze a pig.
Milk a goat.


00:20:16.915 --> 00:20:18.644
Hello?


00:20:18.717 --> 00:20:22.209
Hi. I'm here to tell you
that I won't be working here.


00:20:22.287 --> 00:20:26.485
Oh, Georgia called me about you.


00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:30.722
- Well, aren't you a pretty little thing?
- Fern. Fern.


00:20:31.863 --> 00:20:36.766
I'll just be a moment, dear.
If you'll stay with the phone...


00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:43.601
Very good, Violet. We don't want any
accidents, it confuses the animals. Come along.


00:20:43.675 --> 00:20:47.441
The bathroom's right in here,
you know that, Violet.


00:20:47.512 --> 00:20:48.877
I'm all right.


00:20:48.947 --> 00:20:51.415
No lifting, Izzy.
I'm telling you, I mean it.


00:20:51.483 --> 00:20:54.577
You're not a weightlifter.


00:20:54.653 --> 00:20:56.382
How do you say?


00:20:56.455 --> 00:21:00.414
Hearing the Basque language makes me
feel better, especially when I'm in pain.


00:21:00.492 --> 00:21:05.794
Hear me as your doctor. I'm telling you, no
lifting. No feedbags, no hay bales, no more cows.


00:21:05.864 --> 00:21:09.459
- I have to lift. I'm Basque.
- You're a Basque with a hernia.


00:21:09.534 --> 00:21:12.560
- No lifting, not even your own hat.
- All right...


00:21:12.638 --> 00:21:16.438
Ahem. Hi. I'm the new office girl.


00:21:17.509 --> 00:21:19.500
You're Lilly's daughter?


00:21:19.578 --> 00:21:24.948
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I am Istegui Argitalexei Sarronainda.


00:21:26.184 --> 00:21:29.119
- But you can call me Izzy.
- Mm.


00:21:29.187 --> 00:21:31.587
- Better.
- And you?


00:21:31.657 --> 00:21:34.421
- I'm Rachel. From California.
- Ah...


00:21:34.493 --> 00:21:36.620
California...
the land of fruits and nuts.


00:21:38.096 --> 00:21:41.691
- Signing out.
- I mean it. Let Harlan do your lifting.


00:21:43.001 --> 00:21:45.993
- You know Harlan?
- Yes. Hardest worker I've ever had.


00:21:46.071 --> 00:21:48.266
He lifts like a Basque.


00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:54.438
You tell Harlan that if he's up for a
little danger, then I'd really love a ride.


00:21:58.116 --> 00:21:59.777
OK.


00:21:59.851 --> 00:22:03.446
I will do that. Nice to meet you, Rachel.
Simon.


00:22:03.522 --> 00:22:05.513
- Slowly.
- Slowly, slowly...


00:22:09.895 --> 00:22:12.796
You are the anti-Christ.


00:22:12.864 --> 00:22:16.960
Violet Seymoure
is in the examination room for you, Doctor.


00:22:17.035 --> 00:22:19.230
- Isn't she a beauty?
- Well...


00:22:19.304 --> 00:22:21.272
- Same as Lilly.
- Sure.


00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:23.137
Yeah, mm-hmm.


00:22:24.876 --> 00:22:28.243
- He treats people?
- Unofficially.


00:22:28.313 --> 00:22:32.977
Oh, this is such a relief,
