No reason in hurting her feelings
if we're not even getting married.


00:44:03.841 --> 00:44:06.901
No, no, we're not getting married.
I don't think so.


00:44:06.977 --> 00:44:09.605
- Oh, is that her?
- Harlan?


00:44:10.748 --> 00:44:12.477
Hey.


00:44:12.549 --> 00:44:14.881
- Surprise.
- I'll say.


00:44:14.952 --> 00:44:18.752
I only have a minute.
I have to get back to choir practice.


00:44:18.822 --> 00:44:21.552
- Hello there. Hi.
- Hi.


00:44:21.625 --> 00:44:26.324
June, I want you to meet my friend Rachel.
She works for Dr. Ward across the street.


00:44:26.397 --> 00:44:33.269
And, well, you know Mrs. Randall over on Hillview.
This is her granddaughter visiting from California.


00:44:33.337 --> 00:44:37.171
Rachel Wilcox. She's going to
Vassar in the fall, in New York.


00:44:38.308 --> 00:44:40.071
- Nice to meet you.
- Hi.


00:44:40.144 --> 00:44:42.635
I kissed Harlan.


00:44:44.548 --> 00:44:48.040
- That's what this is about, actually.
- On the mouth?


00:44:48.118 --> 00:44:51.281
No. I wouldn't do that. Not on the mouth.


00:44:52.556 --> 00:44:55.616
What does this mean, Harlan?


00:44:55.693 --> 00:44:57.354
Nothing.


00:44:57.428 --> 00:45:02.832
That's what this means. June, I just wanted to
come down and be 110% honest about all of this...


00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:09.464
Just... Listen, the truth is, I took advantage
of him, OK? He had nothing to do with it.


00:45:09.540 --> 00:45:15.035
I mean, I kissed him. And he wanted to make
sure that nothing came between the two of you.


00:45:15.112 --> 00:45:18.741
And now it's over and done with,
and we're just friends.


00:45:18.816 --> 00:45:22.513
- And that's all that happened?
- Yeah, that's it.


00:45:27.891 --> 00:45:30.359
She, uh, gave me oral sex.


00:45:31.228 --> 00:45:33.219
He's lying.


00:45:36.100 --> 00:45:37.931
But we didn't kiss.


00:45:38.368 --> 00:45:40.427
June.


00:45:40.504 --> 00:45:42.165
Juniper.


00:45:42.239 --> 00:45:43.900
I mean...


00:45:43.974 --> 00:45:44.998
June bug.


00:45:56.453 --> 00:46:01.015
When Dad was dying, nearly dead,
did you ever miss a meal?


00:46:01.091 --> 00:46:03.924
Eat late? Eat early?


00:46:03.994 --> 00:46:06.258
No. Same time.


00:46:07.297 --> 00:46:09.492
Alone.


00:46:09.566 --> 00:46:12.160
I could turn the radio on.


00:46:13.704 --> 00:46:17.572
You're a minute late. Enjoy your meal.
I'm gonna go wait for Rachel.


00:46:17.975 --> 00:46:22.071
Life is much less of a surprise
when it's all timed down.


00:46:25.115 --> 00:46:29.609
This isn't a surprise, Mother.
This is a damn lie.


00:46:51.742 --> 00:46:53.607
Hey.


00:46:53.677 --> 00:46:55.668
Come on, we're here.


00:46:57.815 --> 00:47:03.378
So, the deal is, I can't see you,
talk to you or be anywhere near you?


00:47:04.855 --> 00:47:08.052
I wasn't exactly in the bargaining position.


00:47:10.327 --> 00:47:13.023
It's not fair.


00:47:14.665 --> 00:47:19.193
She's gonna have everyone she knows
watching me from now on.


00:47:21.972 --> 00:47:24.532
You're my only friend.


00:47:28.445 --> 00:47:30.572
OK, fine.


00:47:33.383 --> 00:47:34.350
Rachel...


00:47:40.157 --> 00:47:42.148
OK, well...


00:47:43.227 --> 00:47:44.888
...bye.


00:47:55.539 --> 00:47:57.530
Enjoy yourself?


00:48:02.346 --> 00:48:04.371
Have fun?


00:48:05.115 --> 00:48:08.312
Mom, what are you doing here?
Where's Grandma?


00:48:08.385 --> 00:48:10.683
Went to bed. I waited up for you.


00:48:11.488 --> 00:48:13.319
I have been sitting here for hours


00:48:13.390 --> 00:48:18.350
thinking how is it that I'm ever
gonna be able to forgive you?


00:48:18.428 --> 00:48:20.794
Sometimes I think the same thing
about you.


00:48:22.833 --> 00:48:29.796
And then it occurred to me a while ago
that the only weapon I have left...


00:48:31.108 --> 00:48:33.440
I've used every other...


00:48:37.447 --> 00:48:39.608
is my love for you.


00:48:39.683 --> 00:48:42.481
You could have phoned it in, Mom.


00:48:42.552 --> 00:48:46.545
- I love you.
- Did you practice that in the mirror?


00:48:46.623 --> 00:48:48.318
Wait.


00:48:48.392 --> 00:48:54.388
He thinks of you as his own daughter.
That's what I don't understand. He loves you.


00:48:54.464 --> 00:48:57.900
The question is, does he love you
how he loves me?


00:49:02.272 --> 00:49:04.433
- I want the truth.
- That's why you're here?


00:49:04.508 --> 00:49:06.533
Yeah, say it. Say it!


00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:09.773
He must have said it to you.
Why drive ten hours to hear it again?


00:49:09.846 --> 00:49:12.679
He did say it, and I believe him.


00:49:12.749 --> 00:49:16.276
I want you to say it.


00:49:16.353 --> 00:49:18.082
Rachel!


00:49:19.356 --> 00:49:25.761
I don't think you know the difference anymore,
what's right or wrong,


00:49:25.829 --> 00:49:28.525
what is a lie and what is the truth.


00:49:30.267 --> 00:49:33.259
Yeah, OK, that is my fault.


00:49:33.337 --> 00:49:37.467
I just... I didn't wanna be like my mother,


00:49:37.541 --> 00:49:39.873
with her good and bad and her rules...


00:49:39.943 --> 00:49:43.674
- Tell me what you want me to say.
- He never touched you.


00:49:43.747 --> 00:49:46.375
He never touched me.


00:49:46.450 --> 00:49:48.281
He never climbed on top of me,


00:49:48.352 --> 00:49:52.880
never put his hand on my thigh when your
head was turned at the table at dinner.


00:49:52.956 --> 00:49:56.756
He never put his mouth on my body.
Never, Mom.


00:49:57.794 --> 00:49:59.785
I said it.


00:50:42.339 --> 00:50:45.399
I can't...


00:51:25.982 --> 00:51:27.973
Not right now, Grandma.


00:51:29.519 --> 00:51:31.510
I'm proud of you.


00:51:41.832 --> 00:51:45.393
Yes, such a happy morning.


00:51:45.469 --> 00:51:49.735
Yes, I have to cut your nails. Yes, I do.


00:51:49.806 --> 00:51:53.139
They're getting a little long.


00:52:14.598 --> 00:52:16.964
When did it start?


00:52:17.033 --> 00:52:19.934
- When I was 12.
- When did it stop?


00:52:22.772 --> 00:52:25.832
When a friend of mine
threatened to kill him.


00:52:25.909 --> 00:52:28.343
That's when I was 14.


00:52:28.411 --> 00:52:33.940
He bought me the Mustang on the condition
that I start again, so I crashed it.


00:52:34.017 --> 00:52:36.781
Rachel? Ha-


00:52:38.722 --> 00:52:41.589
Ham and cheese. One's for Simon.


00:52:41.658 --> 00:52:43.649
Here you go.


00:52:45.629 --> 00:52:47.620
Yeah, have a nice day.


00:52:55.172 --> 00:53:00.132
If you're not in for breakfast in 15 minutes,
you'll have to wait for lunch.


00:53:18.762 --> 00:53:20.855
Let's go, kids. It's open.


00:53:22.399 --> 00:53:24.526
Go like this. Ready? Hold my hand.


00:53:24.601 --> 00:53:29.163
You go like this. A circle.
You can use other colors.


00:53:29.239 --> 00:53:31.673
- Good. That's pretty.
- Thanks so much, Rachel.


00:53:31.741 --> 00:53:36.940
- Oh, you're welcome.
- We will not bite Mommy's ear again, will we? No.


00:53:37.013 --> 00:53:39.777
- Bye. Thanks.
- Bye. Good to see you.


00:53:40.650 --> 00:53:44.746
- Thanks, Mr. Wells. I'm sure we'll see you again.
- Thank you, Doc.


00:53:44.821 --> 00:53:46.618
Hello.


00:53:46.690 --> 00:53:48.920
That is $25, sir.


00:53:48.992 --> 00:53:51.984
No. Doc usually just sends me a bill
now and then.


00:53:52.062 --> 00:53:56.260
Unless you've made prior arrangements,
then it's $25, today.


00:53:56.900 --> 00:54:01.064
- Where's Fern?
- She's on vacation. I'm not really sure.


00:54:01.137 --> 00:54:02.798
Cash or check?


00:54:02.872 --> 00:54:08.071
- This is not the way we usually do it around here.
- Well, I'm new.


00:54:08.144 --> 00:54:10.339
It shows.


00:54:10.413 --> 00:54:13.780
I've written "paid in full" on your receipt.


00:54:13.850 --> 00:54:19.880
I'll let you take these as a reminder.
They're copies of your previous unpaid bills.


00:54:19.956 --> 00:54:22.447
- When's Fern coming back?
- No idea.


00:54:22.525 --> 00:54:25.858
- I'll send you a weekly reminder until they're paid.
- Thank you.


00:54:25.929 --> 00:54:28.659
- Welcome.
- I'm not happy, Andy.


00:54:28.732 --> 00:54:30.723
Have a good day.


00:54:31.701 --> 00:54:38.072
Amazing. I haven't got a nickel out of him
in four years, and you get $25 in two minutes.


00:54:38.141 --> 00:54:39.631
I'm good at getting.


00:54:40.243 --> 00:54:42.575
I'll be right with you, Mr. Lynwood.


00:54:48.418 --> 00:54:51.285
How long have you been doing that for?


00:54:52.255 --> 00:54:54.280
Since college.


00:54:54.357 --> 00:54:56.985
It relaxes me. I just play for myself.


00:54:58.061 --> 00:55:01.861
- Have you dated since your wife passed away?
- Hasn't entered my mind.


00:55:04.067 --> 00:55:07.525
- You know, I used to date your mother.
- I know.


00:55:09.172 --> 00:55:12.005
In fact, I was crazy about her.


00:55:12.776 --> 00:55:15.677
Why didn't you marry her,
save us all the trouble?


00:55:15.745 --> 00:55:19.977
Things don't always work out
the way you think they should.


00:55:20.050 --> 00:55:22.314
But you know about that.


00:55:22.385 --> 00:55:26.617
Wait. That's weird.
So you could have been my dad.


00:55:26.690 --> 00:55:28.885
Your dad had a car. I had a cow.


00:55:28.958 --> 00:55:32.416
Huh. It's always about a car.
Pizza's ready.


00:55:40.870 --> 00:55:44.431
At least talk to him long enough
to tell him you're not talking to him.


00:55:44.507 --> 00:55:46.372
Just pick up and hang up.


00:55:46.443 --> 00:55:49.810
Pick up and hang up,
pick up and hang up and so on.


00:55:49.879 --> 00:55:53.212
Do you have anything this size


00:55:53.283 --> 00:55:55.683
that's serrated, hmm?


00:55:55.752 --> 00:55:58.880
He's got thick skin.


00:55:58.955 --> 00:56:00.217
Hmm?


00:56:05.028 --> 00:56:07.496
You know what's hysterical about all this?


00:56:08.431 --> 00:56:10.763
I signed a prenuptial.


00:56:10.834 --> 00:56:13.428
I'm going to end up back here


00:56:13.503 --> 00:56:19.203
with nothing and no one,
living in a place I am not welcome.


00:56:19.275 --> 00:56:22.073
Who says you're not welcome?


00:56:22.879 --> 00:56:24.608
Your face.


00:56:27.050 --> 00:56:30.417
At least he'll be in prison.


00:56:30.487 --> 00:56:33.320
Arnold is one of the best
criminal defense lawyers


00:56:33.390 --> 00:56:35.881
in California, Mother.


00:56:35.959 --> 00:56:42.364
He's not gonna end up anywhere but free,
happy, laughing and playing golf.


00:56:45.435 --> 00:56:47.426
Go with this one.


00:56:55.044 --> 00:56:57.535
So, did you know my real dad?


00:56:59.716 --> 00:57:03.345
He was exactly what you wouldn't want
a daughter to marry.


00:57:03.420 --> 00:57:07.789
Lilly was angry with everybody, even me,
when she left with him.


00:57:07.857 --> 00:57:11.725
- How could you even stand her?
- She reminds me of you.


00:57:11.795 --> 00:57:13.786
I know.


00:57:14.264 --> 00:57:16.425
There.


00:57:18.201 --> 00:57:21.432
- Do you wanna hear something weird?
- Probably not.


00:57:22.639 --> 00:57:25.699
When Arnold held me, I hated the sex.


00:57:27.143 --> 00:57:31.546
But then, sometimes before,
when he just held me,


00:57:33.516 --> 00:57:36.246
I felt loved.


00:57:36.319 --> 00:57:39.254
And I... I mean, how can that be true?


00:57:40.690 --> 00:57:45.024
Maybe the holding part was love, Rachel.
I'm not sure.


00:57:46.963 --> 00:57:49.193
But I know everything else was a lie.


00:57:54.604 --> 00:57:57.835
I'm gonna show you the top to this
stupid thing so we can finish it.


00:57:57.907 --> 00:57:58.999
- I won't look.
- Here.


00:57:59.075 --> 00:58:00.804
I'm not looking.


00:58:00.877 --> 00:58:04.643
How can you do a puzzle,
if you don't know what it looks like?


00:58:04.714 --> 00:58:10.414
It's like telling you how your life will end.
It makes everything in between killing time.


00:58:10.487 --> 00:58:13.513
- Go home.
- I don't wanna go home.


00:58:13.590 --> 00:58:16.388
You can't stay here. Good night.


00:58:34.344 --> 00:58:36.335
Time for bed.


00:59:02.539 --> 00:59:06.134
I found these in the closet.


00:59:07.110 --> 00:59:10.568
I thought they'd be safer there.


00:59:10.647 --> 00:59:17.644
Most people dig out presents they don't like
when the person that gave them comes to visit.


00:59:18.721 --> 00:59:21.417
I don't keep flowers in the house.


00:59:22.292 --> 00:59:25.728
It's two past ten, Mother. Go to bed.


00:59:35.104 --> 00:59:36.765
Oh, come on.


00:59:38.041 --> 00:59:41.772
There was a time you'd have dragged me
by hair for drinking.


00:59:41.844 --> 00:59:45.473
I'm too old. So's your hair.


00:59:45.548 --> 00:59:48.517
That's good.


00:59:53.156 --> 00:59:55.488
These go here.


00:59:55.558 --> 00:59:56.957
Here. There.


01:00:04.500 --> 01:00:05.558
Oh.


01:00:06.936 --> 01:00:07.664
Whoo.


01:00:08.972 --> 01:00:12.237
- Whoo- ooh-ooh.
- Come here. Let me take you to bed.


01:00:12.308 --> 01:00:17.007
You don't get second chances.
Don't try and save me. I'm not savable.


01:00:17.080 --> 01:00:19.674
Everybody's savable. That's the rule.


01:00:19.749 --> 01:00:25.619
Screw your rules. I begged you, "Please,
Mommy" for help at Daddy's funeral.


01:00:25.688 --> 01:00:30.990
And that's when I needed saving, Mother,
but, no, you wouldn't give me a cent.


01:00:31.060 --> 01:00:35.622
- You were drinking.
- I was alone with a four year old. I was scared.


01:00:35.698 --> 01:00:39.156
Arnold saved us. Arnold saved me.


01:00:39.235 --> 01:00:41.863
I wanted you to stay.


01:00:41.938 --> 01:00:44.805
I wanted you to die.


01:00:52.115 --> 01:00:54.447
Not really.


01:00:54.517 --> 01:00:56.178
Just a little.


01:00:57.286 --> 01:00:59.686
Why do you need to hurt her?


01:01:01.224 --> 01:01:03.590
Because you slept with my husband.


01:01:10.867 --> 01:01:13.358
Rachel... Aah!


01:01:13.436 --> 01:01:15.631
Mom?


01:01:15.705 --> 01:01:18.037
Grandma. I need help.


01:01:18.107 --> 01:01:19.972
- I'll handle it.
- I didn't touch her.


01:01:20.043 --> 01:01:22.341
- Don't touch me.
- Go to your room.


01:01:22.412 --> 01:01:27.782
- Why did you let her start again?
- I can handle it. Leave me with her. Go.


01:01:30.853 --> 01:01:32.844
Let me look.


01:01:35.425 --> 01:01:38.724
- Careful of the glass. Can you get up?
- Mm-hmm.


01:01:38.795 --> 01:01:42.060
- I am getting up. Where we going?
- I'm gonna put you in bed...


01:01:42.131 --> 01:01:44.599
and I'm gonna give you an aspirin.


01:01:44.667 --> 01:01:48.262
I'm good. I'm gonna make this. OK.


01:01:48.337 --> 01:01:51.738
I'm gonna...
I'm good...


01:01:51.808 --> 01:01:55.039
- Whoa, I'm gonna throw up.
- Not on the rug.


01:01:55.111 --> 01:01:58.979
Let me help. I've done this before.
Come on, Mom.


01:02:01.350 --> 01:02:05.286
This is good. This is good.


01:02:05.354 --> 01:02:09.791
Lilly, can you make it upstairs
without throwing up, please?


01:02:21.437 --> 01:02:23.428
I am fishing.


01:02:23.506 --> 01:02:26.566
It's just me and my dog.


01:02:27.543 --> 01:02:31.479
And Rachel's not here,
and I'm not happy about it.


01:02:33.816 --> 01:02:36.011
The doctor won't hurt you. It's OK.


01:02:46.229 --> 01:02:49.255
I don't know, Melody.
He seems like a pretty calm pig.


01:02:49.332 --> 01:02:55.100
Yeah, right now, but then, suddenly, he gets
alljumpy, starts running around and squealing,


01:02:55.171 --> 01:02:57.662
and he disrupts the other pigs.


01:02:57.740 --> 01:03:00.334
- You think it's stress?
- Pig stress?


01:03:12.855 --> 01:03:14.846
Slut.


01:03:15.525 --> 01:03:17.356
Slut!


01:03:37.380 --> 01:03:40.577
I gotta get to work.
I got that lasso in for you.


01:03:41.684 --> 01:03:46.678
- He doesn't think I'm pretty. He doesn't like me.
- No, he likes Trouble, on the bench over there.


01:04:00.570 --> 01:04:02.299
Where's Rachel?


01:04:02.371 --> 01:04:04.362
- At Simon's.
- Goody.


01:04:04.440 --> 01:04:07.807
I told her to go there till you're better.
Where you going?


01:04:07.877 --> 01:04:12.143
- I'm going for a drive.
- You're not dressed for a drive.


01:04:12.215 --> 01:04:14.683
I'm thirsty, OK? I'm dying of thirst.


01:04:14.750 --> 01:04:19.881
I'm waking up, I can't stand the feeling.
I'm gonna go buy booze, busybody.


01:04:20.456 --> 01:04:24.688
- It wasn't a question.
- No more drinking in the house. Georgia rule.


01:04:24.760 --> 01:04:29.220
Mother, let me go.
I don't care about your rules. Fuck off.


01:04:30.499 --> 01:04:32.592
Get off me. Get off me!


01:04:36.138 --> 01:04:39.369
All right, all right.


01:04:42.345 --> 01:04:46.645
I called Arnold last night,
and I asked him for a divorce.


01:04:48.217 --> 01:04:50.208
OK, Mother?


01:04:52.788 --> 01:04:54.551
You lost your...


01:04:57.193 --> 01:04:59.184
My mind?


01:05:00.496 --> 01:05:02.293
I'll get the booze.


01:05:02.365 --> 01:05:04.356
Go inside.


01:05:10.806 --> 01:05:12.797
Thank you.


01:05:18.447 --> 01:05:20.642
Have a nice party, Georgia.


01:05:31.594 --> 01:05:33.425
"A in Science" for $2,000, please...


01:05:33.496 --> 01:05:39.867
- Thanks for letting me stay over tonight.
- Well, Georgia thought it might be a good idea.


01:05:40.636 --> 01:05:42.501
What's an Allosaurus?


01:05:42.571 --> 01:05:46.302
- I think it's a good idea.
- "Heraldic Beasts", $400, please.


01:05:46.375 --> 01:05:49.242
I found some perfume under the sink.


01:05:50.313 --> 01:05:52.611
I didn't think you'd mind it.


01:05:53.582 --> 01:05:58.076
- I forgot I still had that.
- It's next to your stash of toilet paper.


01:05:58.154 --> 01:06:01.646
- Every time you change a roll, you see it.
- What's the Loch Ness Monster?


01:06:01.724 --> 01:06:05.387
- No. Doug?
- What's an elephant?


01:06:05.461 --> 01:06:08.897
- Do you ever smell it?
- No, I try not to.


01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:11.866
Do you think she'd want you to?


01:06:11.934 --> 01:06:13.925
- Erika?
- Who is Ginsberg?


01:06:14.003 --> 01:06:15.766
"Poets" for $1200, please.


01:06:15.838 --> 01:06:21.299
Poem containing the line "Perched upon
a bust of Pallas just above my chamber door. "


01:06:21.377 --> 01:06:23.607
- What is "The Raven?"
- Right.


01:06:23.679 --> 01:06:27.206
- "Poets," $1600, please.
- Can I ask you a favor?


01:06:27.283 --> 01:06:29.342
During the commercial.


01:06:30.920 --> 01:06:32.911
Can I hold on to you?


01:06:33.889 --> 01:06:37.017
- Hold on to me?
- Just lean against you.


01:06:39.128 --> 01:06:42.655
I just like to feel somebody next to me.


01:06:42.732 --> 01:06:46.498
- "Beasts" for $1200.
- This animal is on the Lopez family coat of arms,


01:06:46.569 --> 01:06:50.767
probably because the name Lopez
comes from the Latin for it.


01:06:50.840 --> 01:06:53.570
- What is a wolf?
- Kathleen. Yes.


01:06:53.642 --> 01:06:55.837
Can I ask you another favor?


01:06:56.746 --> 01:06:58.304
What?


01:06:58.381 --> 01:07:00.372
Relax.


01:07:04.987 --> 01:07:09.481
I'm gonna go to bed.
There are blankets and pillows in the closet.


01:07:13.829 --> 01:07:16.354
You're gonna have to eat something sometime.


01:07:19.035 --> 01:07:21.196
I'm gonna open the door.


01:07:29.512 --> 01:07:34.108
- Oh, you cut your hair.
- It was getting in the way of my drinking.


01:07:37.219 --> 01:07:41.622
All I remember are Dad's hugs,


01:07:41.690 --> 01:07:43.419
his laugh.


01:07:43.492 --> 01:07:47.121
After all of it, just good things.


01:07:47.196 --> 01:07:49.187
Well, good.


01:07:49.265 --> 01:07:53.463
Why did you try so hard
to take that away from me?


01:07:53.536 --> 01:07:56.096
- Did I?
- Little things.


01:07:56.172 --> 01:07:59.539
We loved to watch TV together,
so you took it away.


01:07:59.608 --> 01:08:03.442
Television was a distraction.
Your grades were slipping.


01:08:03.512 --> 01:08:07.039
Were you afraid how much
Daddy and I were alike?


01:08:07.116 --> 01:08:11.450
How much he relied on me?
How little he wanted from you?


01:08:12.388 --> 01:08:17.382
You know, mostly... I was afraid
you'd run off and marry an idiot,


01:08:17.460 --> 01:08:21.692
lose everything you had a chance at,
just like me.


01:08:23.365 --> 01:08:25.629
I blamed you for his drinking.


01:08:26.769 --> 01:08:28.828
Oh. For yours, too?


01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:31.337
Yeah.


01:08:34.777 --> 01:08:38.679
You know what I don't understand,
along with all the rest of it?


01:08:38.747 --> 01:08:40.738
I haven't got a clue.


01:08:41.851 --> 01:08:45.343
If you ever really loved me.


01:08:45.421 --> 01:08:46.911
Don't be ridiculous.


01:08:46.989 --> 01:08:51.551
No, I mean, just ever.
It wouldn't have to include right now.


01:08:51.627 --> 01:08:53.686
What do you think the rules were?


01:08:53.762 --> 01:08:59.132
Why would I waste my time
on somebody that I didn't care about?


01:09:00.336 --> 01:09:07.071
Yeah. I can't ever remember
you saying it.


01:09:07.643 --> 01:09:09.634
Well, my parents never said it.


01:09:09.712 --> 01:09:12.476
So how do you know if they did?


01:09:13.782 --> 01:09:15.773
I don't.


01:09:25.928 --> 01:09:30.991
I hate that you bought me so many.


01:09:32.735 --> 01:09:35.329
You gonna drink the rest of them?


01:09:36.505 --> 01:09:37.164
No.


01:10:05.067 --> 01:10:07.228
How could I not love you?


01:10:28.023 --> 01:10:28.887
Rachel?


01:10:29.358 --> 01:10:31.417
It's just Dr. Ward today.


01:10:32.928 --> 01:10:38.764
- She just needs a little more exercise, more walks.
- You hear that, Bertha?


01:10:38.834 --> 01:10:42.270
Come on. Hey.
Just have to cut out on the snacking.


01:10:44.306 --> 01:10:46.433
Tell her she's fat.


01:10:46.508 --> 01:10:48.373
You are fat.


01:10:48.444 --> 01:10:53.040
See what I told you?
He's a doctor. It's not just me saying it.


01:10:53.115 --> 01:10:55.106
- Thanks, Dr. Ward.
- Sure.


01:10:58.621 --> 01:11:01.112
You look great with short hair.


01:11:06.595 --> 01:11:09.530
- Where's Rachel?
- It's Saturday. I gave her the day off.


01:11:09.598 --> 01:11:11.998
She went fishing with Harlan.


01:11:15.337 --> 01:11:18.170
I need to stop drinking.


01:11:19.275 --> 01:11:21.266
I'm in no hurry.


01:11:22.244 --> 01:11:26.044
- How can I help?
- She's pregnant, is all.


01:11:28.484 --> 01:11:32.113
Why don't you wait in the office?
This'll take a second.


01:11:37.326 --> 01:11:40.295
She's got that California tan.


01:11:40.362 --> 01:11:44.731
- You think it's real or a spray-on?
- I don't know.


01:11:45.200 --> 01:11:50.934
- It's risky being my friend.
- Well, that's what I was coming around to is...


01:11:51.006 --> 01:11:54.271
maybe we could be more than friends, you know,


01:11:54.343 --> 01:11:57.244
if you thought you could ever sort of...


01:11:58.247 --> 01:11:59.976
I don't know...


01:12:00.049 --> 01:12:01.914
love me?


01:12:06.789 --> 01:12:08.950
I'm kicking men, Harlan.


01:12:10.526 --> 01:12:15.122
No, really. So I guess that's what
I was trying to say... kicking men.


01:12:15.197 --> 01:12:19.531
Yeah, well, I'll be gone for two years
on this mission.


01:12:20.869 --> 01:12:23.463
You can't kick forever, can you?


01:12:25.507 --> 01:12:27.168
I promise I'll write.


01:12:27.876 --> 01:12:32.438
I think they're going. Get on the cellphone.
Call the girls. Let's follow her.


01:12:35.551 --> 01:12:39.851
More kittens.
As if this town needs more cats.


01:12:39.922 --> 01:12:41.913
And that was my last patient.


01:12:45.194 --> 01:12:47.685
Remember the clock tower?


01:12:47.763 --> 01:12:50.994
- I do. Do you?
- Like it was yesterday.


01:12:51.066 --> 01:12:53.159
We changed the clock back.


01:12:53.836 --> 01:12:56.168
Yeah, yeah.


01:12:56.238 --> 01:13:01.039
And the whole day,
the whole town was just a mess.


01:13:02.010 --> 01:13:04.410
Except you. You weren't a mess.


01:13:04.480 --> 01:13:07.040
Anyway, um...


01:13:07.116 --> 01:13:09.448
I need Antabuse.


01:13:10.819 --> 01:13:13.447
That makes you violently ill if you drink.


01:13:13.522 --> 01:13:15.717
I already am violently ill.


01:13:18.160 --> 01:13:21.857
I'm going to Rexburg later.
I'll pick some up.


01:13:21.930 --> 01:13:23.921
Thanks.


01:13:25.634 --> 01:13:27.625
Is that all you need?


01:13:29.838 --> 01:13:32.500
How did I miss what I missed?


01:13:34.877 --> 01:13:36.970
People get busy.


01:13:37.045 --> 01:13:42.449
Too busy to notice
what your husband is doing to your daughter?


01:13:42.518 --> 01:13:44.509
I don't know how you missed that.


01:13:46.488 --> 01:13:48.683
You always tell me the truth.


01:13:49.825 --> 01:13:51.816
Thank you.


01:14:24.693 --> 01:14:27.025
- What was that?
- I'm sorry.


01:14:28.430 --> 01:14:29.522
No...


01:14:31.467 --> 01:14:33.332
Thank you. Thank you.


01:14:34.036 --> 01:14:36.027
I gotta go.


01:15:01.463 --> 01:15:04.159
How long do we have to sit here for?


01:15:05.267 --> 01:15:07.258
Smells like rain.


01:15:08.937 --> 01:15:11.667
OK. Let's do it. Mandy, get ready.


01:15:15.777 --> 01:15:18.075
Give us a break, Grace.


01:15:18.146 --> 01:15:20.137
Let's go.


01:15:22.351 --> 01:15:23.750
Car won't start.


01:15:27.122 --> 01:15:28.316
Whoa. Oh.


01:15:30.959 --> 01:15:34.520
- She's gonna ram us.
- Oh, my God. Get out. Go.


01:15:56.818 --> 01:16:00.379
Hi. Want to introduce myself.
Rachel Wilcox. Nice to meet you.


01:16:00.455 --> 01:16:03.151
- Grace Cunningham.
- Howdy, girls. How you doing?


01:16:03.225 --> 01:16:08.663
Look, I just drove over to tell you
that Harlan and I, we're just friends now.


01:16:08.730 --> 01:16:12.063
Nothing's gonna happen again.
I promise. Scout's honor.


01:16:12.134 --> 01:16:16.537
So you guys can go and do whatever
it is you do, have your summer fun.


01:16:16.605 --> 01:16:20.041
And tell June that we're apart,
even if we're not,


01:16:20.108 --> 01:16:22.702
'cause nothing's gonna happen,
and whatever's happened has happened already,


01:16:22.778 --> 01:16:25.269
so that's the end of it.


01:16:25.347 --> 01:16:29.306
Fine. Then why don't you just go home
and leave us all alone?


01:16:29.885 --> 01:16:34.413
OK, I tried to be nice. Let me put this a
different way, 'cause you're not getting it.


01:16:34.489 --> 01:16:38.255
If you call me a name,
if you throw something at me ever again,


01:16:38.327 --> 01:16:43.162
if I see you talking to Harlan, yelling at
Harlan, having anything at all to do with Harlan,


01:16:43.231 --> 01:16:47.634
I will find all of your boyfriends,
and I will fuck them stupid.


01:16:49.871 --> 01:16:52.601
OK? Get it?


01:16:53.141 --> 01:16:55.609
Thanks for your time.
Have a good summer.


01:16:56.878 --> 01:17:00.871
I am gonna pray for her.


01:17:02.117 --> 01:17:03.141
Harlan.


01:17:59.374 --> 01:18:01.569
Hi. I'm looking for my wife.


01:18:08.250 --> 01:18:11.083
- Whose Ferrari is that?
- My stepfather's here.


01:18:22.497 --> 01:18:24.192
Hey, nice car.


01:18:24.266 --> 01:18:25.927
Rachel...


01:18:28.103 --> 01:18:32.403
Just how badly do you hate me
to have to live with this lie?


01:18:32.474 --> 01:18:34.408
I don't hate you.


01:18:37.112 --> 01:18:40.138
- You're on private property.
- Hi, Georgia. I'm...


01:18:40.882 --> 01:18:42.782
Just give me a moment, OK?


01:18:46.621 --> 01:18:49.089
I shouldn't have agreed to pass you off


01:18:49.157 --> 01:18:52.320
to someone who you don't know
because I didn't have the patience.


01:18:52.394 --> 01:18:56.922
I should've taken the time.
I should've been there.


01:18:56.998 --> 01:18:59.023
What are you doing here?


01:19:02.170 --> 01:19:04.331
- What am I doing here?
- Yeah.


01:19:04.406 --> 01:19:08.934
You called me to tell me you're leaving me,
and then you hang up?


01:19:09.010 --> 01:19:11.740
And you wanna know what I'm doing here?


01:19:13.181 --> 01:19:18.084
If I had touched my daughter,
I wouldn't be here, would I?


01:19:19.955 --> 01:19:22.947
Come on, honey. Please. You...


01:19:24.693 --> 01:19:27.457
You know me better than anyone on earth.


01:19:27.529 --> 01:19:31.260
- She told me...
- What did she tell you? Huh?


01:19:31.333 --> 01:19:35.793
That she wasn't using drugs
when you found LSD in her room? Huh?


01:19:35.871 --> 01:19:40.899
That she wasn't stealing from you
when I found your emerald ring in a pawn shop?


01:19:40.976 --> 01:19:44.935
Or that she hadn't been drinking
when she crashed her car?


01:19:46.081 --> 01:19:48.140
How many lies have I told?


01:19:48.216 --> 01:19:51.117
Oh, please. You're a lawyer.


01:19:51.853 --> 01:19:54.981
I am fighting for my life, goddammit.


01:19:55.056 --> 01:19:57.547
Don't speak to her like that.


01:20:04.633 --> 01:20:05.429
OK.


01:20:07.402 --> 01:20:13.830
If this was something I couldn't change...
an accident, an illness... I'd accept it.


01:20:13.909 --> 01:20:17.003
She would not lie
about something like this.


01:20:18.213 --> 01:20:20.272
Would I?


01:20:22.217 --> 01:20:24.014
I don't know.


01:20:24.085 --> 01:20:26.815
Honey, please. Please.


01:20:29.491 --> 01:20:32.324
Put this in your mouth,
get in your car, and drive.


01:20:32.394 --> 01:20:36.455
I love your daughter, and I love Rachel,
and I would never do anything...


01:20:36.531 --> 01:20:39.796
- What are you doing?
- You do not take the Lord's name in vain.


01:20:39.868 --> 01:20:42.701
You do not fool around
with little girls. Drive.


01:20:42.771 --> 01:20:45.069
I'm not moving.
I am staying right here.


01:20:47.576 --> 01:20:51.569
- Swear to God, I never touched her.
- Save it for the appeal.


01:20:51.646 --> 01:20:56.310
If you don't put that in your mouth soon,
I'm gonna dismantle your car.


01:20:56.384 --> 01:20:58.352
OK.


01:20:59.821 --> 01:21:02.119
I'm leaving. All right?


01:21:05.427 --> 01:21:10.831
I'll be here until Lilly's ready
to come home to San Francisco, OK?


01:21:28.817 --> 01:21:30.785
What if he's innocent?


01:21:30.852 --> 01:21:34.015
Well, it felt really good anyway.


01:21:42.197 --> 01:21:42.891
Rachel...


01:21:44.566 --> 01:21:45.328
Rachel...


01:21:46.868 --> 01:21:50.133
- Can I talk to you?
- No.


01:21:50.205 --> 01:21:52.435
Can you talk to me?


01:21:55.777 --> 01:21:56.505
Rachel.


01:22:01.049 --> 01:22:06.180
I'm at the only motel in this town,
next to the Halfway House Café.


01:22:06.688 --> 01:22:09.521
Lil, just hear me out, please.


01:22:10.558 --> 01:22:15.621
Rachel will get over her anger and take back
this lie one day, but where will you and I be?


01:22:15.697 --> 01:22:20.225
What kind of life will we have led
until that happens?


01:22:20.302 --> 01:22:23.169
I just don't want you to
regret not believing me.


01:22:23.238 --> 01:22:27.766
But I need you here with me, now.


01:22:33.515 --> 01:22:35.449
I don't know who to believe.


01:22:37.118 --> 01:22:41.282
You have to believe that
I wanted her to go to rehab, but, uh...


01:22:41.356 --> 01:22:47.625
you said no, remember? You said you didn't
wanna get into your own demons, right?


01:22:49.898 --> 01:22:52.526
That's true.


01:22:54.803 --> 01:22:57.670
- Can I get you anything?
- No, thank you.


01:22:57.739 --> 01:22:59.866
Nothing? No baked potato special...


01:22:59.941 --> 01:23:02.171
- You're just gonna sit there?
- It's fine.


01:23:02.243 --> 01:23:05.041
I'll take care of you. Thank you.


01:23:08.149 --> 01:23:12.984
I'll do anything
to show you how much I love you


01:23:13.054 --> 01:23:16.820
and how easy it is for me
to forgive her. OK?


01:23:18.626 --> 01:23:22.687
We'll find our way through this.
I know we can.


01:23:22.764 --> 01:23:24.459
Rachel. Oh...


01:23:26.101 --> 01:23:28.899
I didn't know where you were.
Are you OK?


01:23:30.305 --> 01:23:32.773
I'm fine, Grandma.


01:23:34.509 --> 01:23:39.708
I want you to stay there at Simon's.
And I think probably your mom's gonna call.


01:23:39.781 --> 01:23:43.376
- OK?
- Yeah. OK, I'll talk to you later.


01:23:44.185 --> 01:23:47.586
I have to go. I'm cooking Simon dinner.


01:23:47.655 --> 01:23:49.646
I love you, sweetie.


01:24:01.302 --> 01:24:02.997
Hello?


01:24:03.938 --> 01:24:06.406
- Who is it?
- Me.


01:24:11.379 --> 01:24:13.438
Hi.


01:24:13.515 --> 01:24:16.848
- I need a bathroom.
- OK. Are you OK?


01:24:18.386 --> 01:24:21.355
This way. Make a left.
Right here on the left.


01:24:25.827 --> 01:24:27.658
I'll get you water.


01:24:38.540 --> 01:24:40.701
Here you go.


01:24:40.775 --> 01:24:42.402
I...


01:24:43.178 --> 01:24:47.877
It's always so much easier to believe
what you need than what you know.


01:24:47.949 --> 01:24:49.940
I need Arnold.


01:24:51.186 --> 01:24:55.680
He has me convinced.
And you have me convinced.


01:24:58.626 --> 01:25:01.288
He finally got his Ferrari, huh?


01:25:07.969 --> 01:25:10.301
Help me understand.


01:25:11.406 --> 01:25:17.936
I need to just tell you what I feel,
because all I saw was how much you loved him.


01:25:18.012 --> 01:25:20.480
How much he loved you.


01:25:21.950 --> 01:25:24.316
How much he loves me.


01:25:27.455 --> 01:25:30.515
And I thought, "How lucky we are. "


01:25:31.392 --> 01:25:38.457
I just can't fit what he's done
with who I always thought he was.


01:25:41.569 --> 01:25:43.799
I came to tell you I believe you.


01:25:46.274 --> 01:25:48.208
I like your hair short.


01:25:48.276 --> 01:25:52.007
And that none of this is your fault.


01:25:53.381 --> 01:25:55.906
None of this is your fault.


01:26:04.392 --> 01:26:06.986
I really did just say it to make a point.


01:26:10.698 --> 01:26:12.529
What?


01:26:14.702 --> 01:26:18.297
Simon believed me.
Grandma believed me.


01:26:20.375 --> 01:26:23.276
Mom, I just wanted to see if you did.


01:26:32.921 --> 01:26:35.014
Oh, please...


01:26:37.559 --> 01:26:39.823
I screwed up with Vassar.


01:26:39.894 --> 01:26:44.263
I screwed it all up, and I knew
I wasn't ever coming home again.


01:26:44.732 --> 01:26:47.929
And I wanted both of you
to pay for my mistakes.


01:26:50.171 --> 01:26:54.972
You can be mad at me if you want.
And tell him I'm sorry.


01:26:57.178 --> 01:27:00.045
He's not even angry with you.


01:27:00.114 --> 01:27:02.412
He's ready to forgive you.


01:27:11.726 --> 01:27:14.320
I might need a little time.


01:29:13.848 --> 01:29:15.941
It was good. Thank you.


01:29:16.017 --> 01:29:17.917
You're welcome.


01:29:17.985 --> 01:29:23.423
When my mom was too drunk to cook, I used to take
whatever was in the fridge and put it in a pot.


01:29:28.062 --> 01:29:29.962
What's going on?


01:29:31.399 --> 01:29:33.390
Same old thing.


01:29:36.104 --> 01:29:39.301
Your mom called.
She wants to say good night.


01:29:41.275 --> 01:29:43.869
I'm here, home, at Grandma's.


01:29:44.545 --> 01:29:47.412
- Would you come over?
- No.


01:29:48.015 --> 01:29:49.448
OK.


01:29:50.818 --> 01:29:52.308
Well, good night, then.


01:29:52.387 --> 01:29:55.049
Please come back to San Francisco.


01:29:56.157 --> 01:29:58.284
No, Mom, not right now.


01:29:58.960 --> 01:30:02.896
We can't leave it like this.
We have to talk.


01:30:02.964 --> 01:30:06.024
Can you call me in the morning?


01:30:06.768 --> 01:30:08.998
Yeah, OK.


01:30:10.671 --> 01:30:13.831
OK.


01:30:14.442 --> 01:30:16.501
Goodbye.


01:31:12.066 --> 01:31:14.364
You need help, Rachel.


01:31:15.403 --> 01:31:17.337
That's why I'm here.


01:31:17.405 --> 01:31:20.772
You nearly destroyed your mother
with all this, you know.


01:31:20.842 --> 01:31:22.537
I'll pay for your therapy.


01:31:22.610 --> 01:31:24.840
Too late.


01:31:24.912 --> 01:31:32.512
I'll tell you what. I'll leave my Ferrari here,
we'll drive your mother's car back to Frisco,


01:31:32.587 --> 01:31:37.217
and you can have mine for telling
her the truth. How's that sound?


01:31:38.426 --> 01:31:40.690
I'm uncomfortable with you in my room.


01:31:40.761 --> 01:31:43.525
And Gonzales
will have himself a base hit.


01:31:43.598 --> 01:31:45.657
As Garrett Randall steps in...


01:31:47.335 --> 01:31:49.303
OK, here's the deal.


01:31:50.037 --> 01:31:55.168
If Mom goes back with you, loves being with
you, can't live without you, blah-blah-blah,


01:31:55.243 --> 01:31:57.268
then that's the end of it.


01:31:57.345 --> 01:31:58.835
That's the plan?


01:31:58.913 --> 01:32:04.078
Well, if she decides that I'm
lying about lying, then you owe me.


01:32:05.920 --> 01:32:07.911
Owe you what?


01:32:10.691 --> 01:32:13.353
- I'm not gonna take you to court or anything.
- Oh...


01:32:13.427 --> 01:32:16.419
I won't sue you. No newspapers.


01:32:17.031 --> 01:32:20.797
Just write her a letter
saying you're sorry about what you did to me.


01:32:20.868 --> 01:32:23.769
- That's it, huh?
- And a check for ten million.


01:32:24.238 --> 01:32:28.402
Hmm. Oh. Right. That. Of course.


01:32:28.476 --> 01:32:33.778
You always bragged about how much you were
worth while we had our "father-daughter time. "


01:32:33.848 --> 01:32:36.840
Like that would impress me enough
to think it was all OK.


01:32:36.918 --> 01:32:40.319
I really hope you weren't lying.
I hope you're worth 20 million.


01:32:40.388 --> 01:32:44.757
Because if she decides you're a piece of shit,
which you are, she gets ten.


01:32:46.127 --> 01:32:47.924
OK.


01:32:48.329 --> 01:32:50.695
I'll see you in court.


01:32:53.467 --> 01:32:56.027
Along with the videotape.


01:32:57.238 --> 01:32:59.297
What are you talking about?


01:33:01.475 --> 01:33:05.844
- You know, I hate this smell.
- What are you talking about?


01:33:05.913 --> 01:33:09.371
Remember Tommy?
The one that stuck the gun to your head?


01:33:09.450 --> 01:33:12.248
What are you, wired?
You have a tape on, is that it?


01:33:12.320 --> 01:33:14.720
No, nothing. Honest.


01:33:16.524 --> 01:33:19.425
All right, that's enough, Rachel.


01:33:22.964 --> 01:33:27.526
The thing is, I had him record us.
He has a videotape of us.


01:33:27.602 --> 01:33:29.467
Oh, really?


01:33:29.537 --> 01:33:35.134
You, you're all sweaty and grunting
and pushing. And me, I'm 14.


01:33:35.776 --> 01:33:37.471
Right.


01:33:38.045 --> 01:33:44.075
Look, as long as my mother's happy, you win
everything. I won't even hold it against you.


01:33:44.919 --> 01:33:47.217
- Keep my mother happy, OK?
- OK.


01:33:57.832 --> 01:33:59.595
You were thinking?


01:33:59.667 --> 01:34:01.464
I have a little money saved.


01:34:01.535 --> 01:34:07.201
I'd be glad to pay Rachel's way through
college, you know, if that's ever a problem.


01:34:08.275 --> 01:34:10.903
Or if she doesn't need it,
I could let you have it.


01:34:10.978 --> 01:34:15.005
Use it for a down payment on a house,
if that's ever a problem.


01:34:18.853 --> 01:34:21.822
Mom, I'm leaving in the morning with Arnold.


01:34:28.295 --> 01:34:30.286
Thank you.


01:35:37.398 --> 01:35:39.593
Go back to the couch.


01:35:40.167 --> 01:35:42.260
I love you.


01:35:44.872 --> 01:35:47.067
- Please, Simon.
- No.


01:35:48.509 --> 01:35:50.909
It's not like you're family.


01:35:50.978 --> 01:35:54.106
I'm never gonna have sex with you,
all right? Ever.


01:35:54.181 --> 01:35:56.308
No.


01:35:56.383 --> 01:36:00.615
It's not like I haven't thought about it.
You know, it's hard not to.


01:36:00.688 --> 01:36:04.146
You're good at it, this attracting men thing.


01:36:04.225 --> 01:36:07.820
And you're beautiful and funny and bright.
Goddamn him for this!


01:36:07.895 --> 01:36:09.624
This has nothing to do with him.


01:36:09.697 --> 01:36:13.827
He tried to take away all the things that
would let you love me like a friend or a father.


01:36:13.901 --> 01:36:16.699
This has everything to do with him.


01:36:19.540 --> 01:36:25.843
This is about knowing the difference between
right and wrong, between the truth and a lie.


01:36:25.913 --> 01:36:28.177
He took that from you.


01:36:28.249 --> 01:36:32.185
And if you can't tell the difference,
then you can't trust anyone.


01:36:34.789 --> 01:36:37.349
And if you can't trust, you can't love.


01:36:41.896 --> 01:36:44.797
What's it like to be so sure of yourself?


01:36:44.865 --> 01:36:46.958
It's good.


01:36:51.572 --> 01:36:53.938
Tell me about your wife.


01:36:54.008 --> 01:36:56.101
Describe it for me.


01:37:00.681 --> 01:37:02.342
Describe what?


01:37:03.751 --> 01:37:05.912
How you loved her.


01:37:07.221 --> 01:37:12.989
When I touched her,
I felt the best part of me being touched.


01:37:15.930 --> 01:37:19.024
It's just a different kind of love, Rachel.


01:37:19.867 --> 01:37:22.734
Do you think you'll ever have it again?


01:37:23.904 --> 01:37:25.371
No.


01:37:26.407 --> 01:37:28.500
Maybe. I don't know.


01:37:29.677 --> 01:37:31.508
Maybe.


01:37:33.814 --> 01:37:36.612
Thanks. For saying no.


01:37:54.101 --> 01:37:56.035
Where's your car?


01:37:56.103 --> 01:37:58.071
Around the corner.


01:37:58.806 --> 01:38:00.535
For safety reasons.


01:38:02.443 --> 01:38:06.072
If I could lock the windows and doors
and keep her from you, I would.


01:38:06.146 --> 01:38:08.239
I'll wait for her right here.


01:38:13.921 --> 01:38:16.014
You know I know.


01:38:16.090 --> 01:38:18.558
Come on, Georgia.


01:38:18.993 --> 01:38:23.555
I don't care what Rachel says. I know.
And that must eat at you.


01:38:24.732 --> 01:38:27.826
Having something that disgusting, criminal,


01:38:28.702 --> 01:38:31.762
known out here, exposed,
out in the open.


01:38:34.408 --> 01:38:39.471
If my daughter wasn't in love with you,
I would kill you.


01:38:44.818 --> 01:38:48.754
I've been calling Rachel for over an hour.
It's still busy.


01:38:48.822 --> 01:38:50.653
Thank you.


01:38:50.724 --> 01:38:56.822
Would you give this to her? I didn't seal it.
You can read it if you want to.


01:39:01.201 --> 01:39:03.431
I don't want you to go.


01:39:10.044 --> 01:39:12.376
I'll call you when I get home.


01:39:12.446 --> 01:39:15.677
I noticed the glass bedpan on your mantel.


01:39:16.283 --> 01:39:18.342
Yeah, I found room for it.


01:39:18.919 --> 01:39:20.477
Thank you.


01:39:33.367 --> 01:39:35.494
Hey, boys.


01:39:35.569 --> 01:39:37.901
Come say goodbye to Lilly.


01:39:40.574 --> 01:39:42.132
- Bye.
- Bye, Lilly.


01:39:42.209 --> 01:39:44.837
Goodbye. Goodbye.


01:40:12.339 --> 01:40:14.705
Who is it?


01:40:14.775 --> 01:40:16.834
Coming.


01:40:19.913 --> 01:40:22.746
Why didn't you answer the phone?


01:40:22.816 --> 01:40:24.647
I just woke up.


01:40:24.718 --> 01:40:28.154
Simon's at work already.
Did they leave yet?


01:40:31.658 --> 01:40:34.752
I thought I could let it go, but I can't.


01:40:34.828 --> 01:40:37.422
Rachel, you lied to her.


01:40:38.632 --> 01:40:42.466
I put together a puzzle
without looking at the box.


01:40:42.536 --> 01:40:44.265
- Look at me.
- Why?


01:40:44.338 --> 01:40:47.364
Look at me. You have to tell her the truth.


01:40:48.442 --> 01:40:52.606
Simon says I don't know the difference
between the truth and a lie.


01:40:52.679 --> 01:40:55.648
- Can a lie ever be right?
- No.


01:40:57.217 --> 01:40:59.378
And what happens if I tell the truth?


01:40:59.953 --> 01:41:02.444
We're gonna press criminal charges.


01:41:02.523 --> 01:41:05.515
But it's gonna take the three of us.
Come on, get dressed.


01:41:05.592 --> 01:41:08.425
- What makes you think we'll catch them?
- Well, we'll try.


01:41:08.495 --> 01:41:11.328
Simon and Harlan are in the truck.
She gave me this for you.


01:41:11.398 --> 01:41:13.593
- No, no. Go get dressed.
- OK.


01:41:13.667 --> 01:41:15.464
You can read this on the way. Hurry.


01:41:15.536 --> 01:41:20.564
- What makes you think she'll believe me now?
- We'll make her, you and I.


01:41:30.551 --> 01:41:35.750
- Maybe I should've driven myself.
- Then I would've been tailgating you.


01:41:40.394 --> 01:41:42.419
What's your hurry?


01:41:47.367 --> 01:41:50.928
Sending someone back
for your car is ridiculous.


01:41:51.004 --> 01:41:54.940
I might not even do that.
It's all too much trouble.


01:41:55.542 --> 01:41:59.034
Can't leave your car parked
on some side street in Idaho.


01:41:59.113 --> 01:42:03.777
Pull over. You know you want to.
It's the right thing to do.


01:42:05.152 --> 01:42:07.484
Rachel can have it if she wants.


01:42:09.523 --> 01:42:11.047
- Rachel?
- Mm-hmm.


01:42:12.793 --> 01:42:17.355
You love that car.
You waited eight months for that car.


01:42:17.431 --> 01:42:22.459
I don't hold any of this against her, honey.
I want her to know that.


01:42:26.507 --> 01:42:29.237
Come on, let's go. Let's go.


01:42:34.148 --> 01:42:36.116
Pull over.


01:42:36.183 --> 01:42:39.243
What? What's the matter?
You sick or something?


01:42:39.319 --> 01:42:42.880
Did you think your Ferrari
would be payment enough for her?


01:42:42.956 --> 01:42:47.086
- What? That's not what this is about.
- Get me outta here. Pull over.


01:42:47.161 --> 01:42:50.790
- Come on, honey. Please.
- Pull over right now!


01:42:50.864 --> 01:42:53.264
All right, all right! I'm off. Stop it!


01:42:53.333 --> 01:42:59.795
Honey, stop. Lilly, stop it!
All right, I'm doing it! I'm pulling over!


01:43:06.413 --> 01:43:08.381
Goddammit, Lilly.


01:43:09.283 --> 01:43:10.910
Talk to me.


01:43:12.553 --> 01:43:14.851
Will you please turn around?


01:43:16.089 --> 01:43:18.387
Turn around!


01:43:19.026 --> 01:43:21.551
All right, fine. Keep walking.


01:43:24.798 --> 01:43:26.823
There's your life.


01:43:26.900 --> 01:43:30.301
Back in Idaho. With your mother.


01:43:37.010 --> 01:43:39.069
She seduced me.


01:43:47.854 --> 01:43:49.481
Naah!


01:43:51.458 --> 01:43:53.119
You lying son of a bitch!


01:43:53.193 --> 01:43:57.527
What did you expect me to do
while you were in your drunken stupor?


01:43:57.598 --> 01:43:59.259
And guess what.


01:43:59.333 --> 01:44:01.096
She enjoyed it.


01:44:04.671 --> 01:44:09.973
You wanna take this to trial?
You go right ahead. I welcome it.


01:44:10.043 --> 01:44:13.410
You're going to jail, you sick bastard.


01:44:18.785 --> 01:44:21.447
You can bet on it, pervert.


01:44:32.833 --> 01:44:40.035
"Dear Rachel, my mother always told me the hardest
things to do in life are to trust, to have faith,


01:44:40.107 --> 01:44:42.268
and to forgive. "


01:44:42.909 --> 01:44:48.404
"So I want you to hear the strength
in my voice when I say I forgive you,


01:44:48.482 --> 01:44:50.814
because I love you. "


01:44:50.884 --> 01:44:53.478
"That simple and that complicated. "


01:44:53.553 --> 01:44:59.116
"To forgive is to move forward.
Georgia rule. Love, Mom. "


01:45:46.073 --> 01:45:48.268
I'm sorry, Mommy.


01:45:49.643 --> 01:45:52.237
Oh, bunny. Oh, bunny.


01:45:53.847 --> 01:45:55.940
I love you.


01:45:59.286 --> 01:46:01.345
I'm so sorry.


01:46:06.193 --> 01:46:08.559
Ms. Randall.


01:46:08.628 --> 01:46:12.758
I think you should know
that I'm in love with your granddaughter.


01:46:12.833 --> 01:46:18.430
And, well, when I get back from my mission,
I fully intend to marry her.


01:46:18.505 --> 01:46:20.234
OK.

